     3	
     4	## Banhall
     5	
     6	SR&ED report generation for a consulting firm. SvelteKit 2 + Svelte 5 runes, Tailwind, Convex backend, Claude/OpenRouter via `convex/ai/`. Domain contract in `docs/product-domain.md`, AI target architecture in `docs/ai-architecture-plan.md`, current findings in `docs/ai-engine-audit-2026-08-25.md`. Tickets live in futur-board (BNH-*), not this repo.
     7	
     8	## Policy
     9	
    10	- Never repurpose `projects.createdBy`, mix human workflow with generation state, or invent transitions/permissions outside `docs/product-domain.md` without recording an approved amendment there.
    11	- Agents propose, humans apply: no code path may let an AI tool mutate report prose directly; route through `chatProposals` + `applyProposal`.
    12	- Never hand-edit `convex/_generated/`.
    13	
    14	## Where things are
    15	
    16	- Convex code: read `convex/_generated/ai/guidelines.md` first; it overrides training-data Convex patterns.
    17	- Frontend conventions and convex-svelte idioms: `docs/svelte-migration.md`.
    18	- Design tokens: `src/routes/layout.css`; rules in `docs/design-system.md`; live at `/styleguide`.
    19	- Changelog entries: `docs/changelog-guidelines.md`.
    20	
    21	## Running and verifying
    22	
    23	- One command proves a change: `bash scripts/loop-verify.sh`. Numbered steps: preflight, Convex typecheck, `npm run check`, `npm test`, the test-discovery guard, `npm run build`, the two client-uploader harnesses. Browser-free by default.
    24	- Preflight defaults `PUBLIC_CONVEX_URL` and `PUBLIC_CONVEX_SITE_URL` to public placeholders when unset, so no deployment is needed; it also fails at step 1 naming a missing `node`/`npm`/`pwsh`/`git`.
    25	- Run `npm ci` in each fresh checkout and after dependency changes. The gate only bootstraps an empty `node_modules`; an existing directory does not establish installation freshness or ownership.
    26	- `VERIFY_COMPONENT=1 bash scripts/loop-verify.sh` adds the browser component suite (`npm run test:component`), which needs `npx playwright install chromium` once (Linux: `npx playwright install --with-deps chromium`). Optional preflight launches headless Chromium. `npm test` itself never touches a browser.
    27	- CI defines two jobs: one runs `bash scripts/loop-verify.sh`, the other installs Chromium and runs `npm run test:component`. Still run `test:component` locally before touching `src/lib/components`. Required branch-protection checks are configured separately from this workflow.
    28	
    29	
    30	## Conventions that differ from defaults
    31	
    32	- No JSX, React hooks, or Next.js APIs; Svelte 5 runes only.
    33	- Use design-system type roles and the remapped gray ramp; never ad-hoc hex values.
    34	- Max font weight 500 in new or redesigned UI; hierarchy via size and ink color, not bold.
    35	- Use bits-ui/shadcn-svelte primitives over native `<select>`/`<input>` controls.
    36	- Active tab = primary fill + white text; inactive hover = primary wash.
    37	
    38	## Known pitfalls
    39	
    40	- `exportTemplateDocx` is not SSR-safe; import it only inside browser-only code paths.
    41	- Never add `sveltekit()` to `vitest.component.config.ts`; it pulls `$app`/`$env` and breaks the browser project.
    42	
    43	<!-- /bmad:context -->
